  "content_blocks": [
    {
      "block_id": "b00000",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Setting time limits",
      "ordinal": 0,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00001",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In: Procure > Clarification and due diligence",
      "ordinal": 1,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00002",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Overview",
      "ordinal": 2,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00003",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "This regulation requires contracting authorities to take into account the complexity of the contract and the time required for preparing tenders when setting relevant time limits during the procurement process (notwithstanding minimum time limits required by procurement procedures under regulations 27 to 33 of the PCR 2015). In particular, where it is necessary for bidders to carry out site visits or inspections in order to prepare their tenders, this must be reflected accordingly by the contracting authority when setting time limits.",
      "ordinal": 3,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00004",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "In the event that significant changes are made to the procurement documents, or additional information, despite being requested in good time, is provided within six days of the tender submission deadline (four days for accelerated procedures), contracting authorities must extend the tender submission deadline by an amount which is proportionate to the importance of the change or information. Such extension is not required where additional information does not impact on the preparation of tenders or has not been requested by suppliers in good time.",
      "ordinal": 4,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Overview"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00005",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Objective at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 5,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00006",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "The tender submission deadline must be extended by a proportionate period where significant changes are made to the procurement documents, or where additional information (despite being requested in good time) is provided to bidders within six days of the tender submission deadline.",
      "ordinal": 6,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Objective at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00007",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Key considerations at this commercial stage",
      "ordinal": 7,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00008",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "Contracting authorities should:",
      "ordinal": 8,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00009",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that the tender submission deadline is extended by a proportionate period where additional information is revealed within six days of the tender submission deadline, despite being requested in good time (four days in the case of accelerated procedures), or where significant changes are made to the procurement documents",
      "ordinal": 9,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00010",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "ensure that all relevant information is made available at the outset of the procurement process to mitigate the risk of requiring extension(s) to the tender submission deadline.",
      "ordinal": 10,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Key considerations at this commercial stage"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00011",
      "block_type": "heading",
      "text": "Legal framework",
      "ordinal": 11,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00012",
      "block_type": "p",
      "text": "See also in the Procurement Act 2023:",
      "ordinal": 12,
      "heading_path": [
        "Setting time limits",
        "Legal framework"
      ],
      "source_locator": null,
      "metadata": {}
    },
    {
      "block_id": "b00013",
      "block_type": "li",
      "text": "Section 31: Modifying a section 19 procurement",
      "ordinal": 13,
